KDE's kimpanel implementation for GNOME Shell

Install requirements
gettext
cmake

If you'd like to install it as user, run ./install.sh under the root of source.

Translation: https://www.transifex.com/fcitx/fcitx/gnome-shell-extensions-kimpanel/

Wayland and focus-follows-mouse
-----------------------------

With GNOME's strict `mouse` focus mode, moving the pointer over a candidate
panel can clear the application's keyboard focus. This can interrupt preedit,
make the candidate panel flash, and leave raw input or spaces in the application.

If you use focus-follows-mouse on Wayland, use `sloppy` mode to retain the last
focused window while the pointer is over the candidate panel or desktop:

    gsettings set org.gnome.desktop.wm.preferences focus-mode 'sloppy'

Windows will still receive focus when the pointer enters them. This changes
the desktop focus preference; the extension does not change it automatically.
